id: pm-gh1610
title: "GH-1610: compact lean refusals and expose structured claim context"
description: "GitHub report https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1610 measures redundant refusal headlines and generic recovery boilerplate, with lean text larger than default. Investigate current public SDK normalization and renderers, preserve actionable recovery, and expose existing claim holder metadata as typed fields. Reported2026.10.27 behavior has not been independently reproduced; earlier completed lean-error work remains completed."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[2]: agent-ux,github
created_at: "2026-10-27T10:20:14.486Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-31T09:14:59.888Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-31T01:52:15.075Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-31T01:52:15.075Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Reproduce the reported claim-conflict bytes in isolated trackers; remove duplicated and constant lean boilerplate without deleting specific recovery; preserve default compatibility and sensitive-value redaction; verify CLI and public SDK structured holder metadata; add meaningful before/after controls.
value: Reduce repeated agent refusal context while retaining executable recovery
impact: CLI text and structured SDK refusal consumers
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "The SDK declares the constant refusal boilerplate once (PM_GENERIC_REFUSAL_GUIDANCE, PM_RECOVERY_ECHO_FIELDS, isGenericRefusal*, projectLeanRecoveryPayload) and both lean projections consume it: lean text drops the generic requirement, generic why, pm --help examples and the invocation echo while keeping next steps, specific recovery and verifier findings; lean JSON drops generic required/examples and the recovery echo on top of title/why. Text refusals no longer repeat a single-line message under What happened. already_claimed_by carries item_id, claimed_by, claimed_at and claim_source in PmCliErrorContext, the JSON envelope and the classification (resolveItemOwnershipConflict is public), rendered in text as Held by: <holder> (<source> since <time>)."
expected_result: Lean refusals preserve code-specific recovery and typed claim metadata while never exceeding equivalent default output; shared SDK normalization owns semantics.
actual_result: "Isolated-tracker claim conflict: text 798 -> 719 bytes, --lean text 813 -> 494, --json 1,172 -> 1,299 (typed holder fields added), --json --lean 968 -> 648; an invalid-value refusal 771 -> 602 under --lean. Property test over six refusal codes: lean never larger than default (text and JSON) and no non-label line shared by every lean output. Claim-conflict tests assert claimed_by/claim_source (claim vs assignment) and claimed_at (ISO, null on corrupt history). refusal.exit_code is retained because refusal is the stable identity used by the refusal-closure tooling. Agent-task-token, refusal-closure, docs-skills, static quality gates and the linked test run pass."
